B8hUk0K5Whpiki69E9IXSE6Oqp_ZeRQMHKH4SQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# EDITORIAL_FEEDBACK.md — News Card Editorial Feedback\n\nHandles Telegram feedback on published news cards. **Not part of the crypto pipeline.**\n\n---\n\n## When this applies\n\n| Pattern | Example |\n|---------|---------|\n| Callback `oc_r:` / `oc_ri:` / `oc_ri_menu:` | Rate article or image |\n| Callback `oc_draft:` / `oc_draft_yes:` / `oc_draft_no:` | Unpublish flow |\n| Callback `oc_publish:` / `oc_publish_yes:` / `oc_publish_no:` | Publish flow |\n| Callback `oc_edit:` / `oc_edit_apply:` / `oc_edit_cancel:` | Edit flow |\n| Text | `RATE 8`, `IMAGE 7`, `DRAFT`, `PUBLISH`, `EDIT`, `REVISION RETRY` |\n| Text reply to edit prompt | Editorial feedback (what to change) |\n\n---\n\n## What to do\n\n1. **Do NOT** start or continue the crypto news pipeline.\n2. **Do NOT** spawn subagents — **except** the mandatory writer revision block below.\n3. Run the handler immediately:\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/handle_card_feedback.py \\\n  --payload \"<callback data if present>\" \\\n  --message-text \"<user text if present>\" \\\n  --chat-id \"<telegram chat id>\" \\\n  --user-id \"<telegram user id>\" \\\n  --username \"<telegram username if known>\" \\\n  --reply-to-message-id \"<replied-to message id if present>\"\n```\n\n4. **If the handler already sent a Telegram reply, do NOT repeat stdout in the group — end turn silently** — **unless** stdout is `EDIT_REVISION_PENDING` (see revision block; you must continue in the same turn).\n5. If handler failed before replying, show the stdout line to the user.\n\n---\n\n## Pipeline vs feedback\n\n| User says | Route |\n|-----------|-------|\n| `run pipeline`, `run crypto news pipeline` | SOUL.md pipeline |\n| RATE, IMAGE, DRAFT, PUBLISH, EDIT, callback taps, edit feedback text | This doc |\n\nPipeline takes precedence only when the message explicitly requests the pipeline.\n\n---\n\n## EDIT flow (text feedback → writer revision)\n\n1. Tap **Edit** or reply `EDIT` to the news card.\n2. Bot asks you to **reply with what to change** (no file download).\n3. Writer revises the article; bot sends **diff summary + Google Doc link + Apply/Cancel**.\n4. Tap **Apply to WordPress** to push live (or **Cancel**).\n5. After apply on a draft → bot offers a **Publish** button.\n\n**Stuck revision?** Reply `REVISION RETRY` or tap **Edit** again while revision is pending.\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL — Writer revision block (same turn)\n\n**When handler stdout is `EDIT_REVISION_PENDING: ta-xxx` OR DB has `revision_pending` for this article:**\n\n**Do NOT end turn / NO_REPLY until steps 0–5 complete or fail.**\n\n### Step 0 — Pre-flight\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/finalize_editorial_revision.py \\\n  --alert-id ta-xxx --preflight-only\n```\n\nIf not `EDIT_REVISION_PREFLIGHT_OK` → tell user artifacts are missing; stop.\n\nLoad revision details:\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/editorial_db.py --get-revision ta-xxx\n```\n\nParse JSON for `run_dir` and `feedback_text`.\n\n### Step 1 — Touch revision stamp\n\n```bash\ndate +%s > \"$RUN_DIR/.revision_started\"\n```\n\n(Use `run_dir` from step 0 JSON.)\n\n### Step 2 — Spawn writer\n\nUse `sessions_spawn` and `sessions_yield` with:\n\n```\nREVISION MODE for {alert_id}.\nRUN_DIR: {run_dir}\nRead {run_dir}/research/validated.json and current article at {run_dir}/article/final.md.\nEditor feedback: \"{feedback_text}\"\nRevise the article per feedback. Keep COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md rules. Length: 1000-1200 body words (aim 1100).\nWrite full article to {run_dir}/article/raw.md. Yield SUCCESS only.\n```\n\n### Step 3 — Finalize\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/finalize_editorial_revision.py \\\n  --alert-id ta-xxx\n```\n\n### Step 4 — End turn\n\n- `EDIT_REVISION_READY` → end turn silently (Telegram already updated).\n- `EDIT_REVISION_FAILED` / `EDIT_REVISION_UNCHANGED` → show outcome; optional **one** writer repair for validation failures only.\n\n---\n\n## PUBLISH flow notes\n\n- Tap **Publish** or reply `PUBLISH` to the card.\n- Confirm with **Yes, publish** / **Cancel**.\n- Sets WordPress post status to `publish` (live on site).\n- If already published → bot replies \"already published\".\n\n---\n\n## DRAFT flow notes\n\n- Tap **Unpublish** or reply `DRAFT` to the card.\n- Confirm with **Yes, unpublish** / **Cancel**.\n- Sets WordPress post status to `draft`.\n\n---\n\n## Mention rules\n\n- Callback taps: no `@mention` needed.\n- Reply to news card: `RATE`, `DRAFT`, `PUBLISH`, `EDIT` work without `@mention`.\n- Reply to bot edit prompt with feedback text: works via `reply_to_bot` or open `awaiting_feedback` session.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779708896259}}
